From 326374cbdce7b95e78ca1d57e9be27a12f227afc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:37:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rpi-firmwared: boot steps on our firmware's boot screen with
 QUIET=1

Quiet boot (redox-rpi #518) with our firmware: the boot screen stays on
HDMI until the login, and Redox's steps show on it through tag
0x000f0002 (rpi-open-firmware #43, #77): percent, flags (failed, last)
and a line of text.

- rpi-firmwared serves a write-only file bootstep: a line
  `PCT [fail] [last] TEXT` sends one step. Only with QUIET set
  (inherited by 40_rpi-firmwared.service); without it a write does
  nothing. If the firmware does not draw the step (no bit 31, length
  below 4, or answer 0: Broadcom's start.elf, QEMU, no HDMI), it logs
  one line and answers EIO to this and every later write in this boot.
  After the last step it sends nothing more.
- `rpi-firmwared step PCT [fail] [last] TEXT` writes such a line and
  ignores EIO, so init can call it. rpi-firmwared is now also in
  /usr/bin for the steps after the switch to the root file system.
- Steps: drivers (25 %, initfs), file system (50 %, initfs), services
  (75 %), network (90 %, only if it comes before the login), and the
  last step "login" (100 %), which fbcond@ waits for, so it comes before
  the first console draws.
- inputd's quiet-boot fallback (no console after 60 s) sends
  `- fail last boot stopped` before it shows the boot log, so no late
  step draws over the log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
